ellie_sales: Quick sync — BigBank wants a POC that uses streaming responses + function/tool calling and strict structured JSON output for downstream ingestion. They're also asking for: reserved pricing (monthly commit + burst), SOC2 evidence, and on-prem/network options. Can we confirm what we can hand them by EOD?

raj_engineering: Got it. Main integration questions to clarify: 1) do they need SSE or websocket? 2) do they expect function calls to be synchronous (tool call in stream) or post-hoc? 3) which fields are required in the structured output schema?

ellie_sales: They prefer SSE for real-time updates, and they want function/tool calls to be invoked during the stream (so the app can act immediately). Structured schema: minimal: {"id": string, "intent": string, "entities": array}. They also want schema validation on our side if possible.

raj_engineering: We can support SSE + streaming function calls. For schema validation we can enforce a mode where the model returns a single stable JSON object at the end of the stream or emits well-formed partial JSON chunks. Example SSE pattern in our JS SDK:```js
const res = await client.stream.create({ model: 'open-llm-rl', input: '...', stream: true, functions: [...] });
for await (const chunk of res.stream()) {
  // chunk can be tokens, partial json, or function-invoke event
  handle(chunk);
}
```
If they need immediate function invocation, include a function definition in the call and watch for `function_call` events in the stream.

maria_security: For SOC2 + privacy: we can provide SOC2 Type II summary, data flow diagram, and our DSP/processor agreements. If BigBank requires on-prem, we need to discuss Redwood Private (customer-managed control plane). Also need to know the data residency region and retention window.

ellie_sales: They're asking for EU residency and 90-day retention. Also want confirmation that KV/prefix caching will not persist PII by default.

kevin_sre: Caching: by default prefix/KV caches are scoped to the model instance and TTL. For POC, we can disable caching in the route config: `cache: { enabled: false }`. Also we can run the POC on Dedicated reserved capacity to guarantee no multi-tenant cache sharing.

leo_customer_success: On the ops side, propose this plan: 1) provide a short sample repo + SSE runbook (we'll hand them a sandbox token), 2) send SOC2 packet + DPA, 3) provide a 2-week Dedicated trial with burst to test QPS. Do we have pricing ranges to share?

ellie_sales: Pricing ask: they want committed 4x A10g-equivalent GPUs for 6 months with burst. Can we give a ballpark for commit + per-token overage + burst hourly?

raj_engineering: Ballpark (internal): commit monthly = $XXk (depends on GPU type), per-token rates scale with quantization/throughput; for streaming workloads it's often cheaper to recommend lower precision quantized model and batching rules. I'll pull model/quant profiles. For burst, we can enable autoscale up to 2x for short windows; charge is hourly for extra nodes. I will draft numbers and attach.

maria_security: Also need to run our standard security questionnaire back-and-forth. Ellie, please ask BigBank to fill the vendor security matrix. I'll pre-populate answers for anything Redwood-managed and mark items requiring legal review (e.g., subprocessor list).

ellie_sales: Will request the matrix. Raj — can you prepare a minimal sample that demonstrates: SSE streaming + an in-stream function call trigger + final structured JSON validation? Prefer a tiny Node example we can ship.

raj_engineering: On it. I'll push a minimal repo by EOD to https://git.redwood.internal/presales/bigbank-poc (sandbox link) and include: 
- node sse client example
- sample function definition and handler (shows tool call in-stream)
- `schema.json` with JSON Schema and local validator snippet using ajv
Snippet:```js
// validate final payload
const Ajv = require('ajv');
const schema = require('./schema.json');
const ajv = new Ajv();
const valid = ajv.validate(schema, finalPayload);
if (!valid) console.error(ajv.errors);
```

deploy-bot: deploy: sandbox token created for project `bigbank-poc-sandbox` (expires in 14 days).

leo_customer_success: Great. Action items: 1) ellie request security matrix + residency confirmation, 2) raj publish sample repo + pricing draft, 3) maria assemble SOC2 + DPA fragments, 4) kevin prepare Dedicated trial setup notes. I'll schedule a 30m demo with BigBank technical folks tomorrow 10am CET.

ellie_sales: Thanks — I'll coordinate and share updates here. :thumbsup:
